● The default pool is already btrfs. The volumes in the compose file just need
  to reference it — x-incus-storage: default is already set. The volumes:
  declarations at the bottom create named volumes which incus-compose maps to
  btrfs subvolumes in the default pool. That's correct as-is.

  The only thing to change is the type: bind mount for mosquitto.conf — that's a
  host path bind, which is fine. The named volumes (nm-sqldata, etc.) will be
  btrfs subvolumes automatically.

  Let me verify what incus-compose does with the volumes: section and
  x-incus-storage:

  Read 1 file, ran 2 shell commands (ctrl+o to expand)

● The pool comes from driver_opts.pool on the volume, or falls back to
  x-incus-storage on the service, or defaults to "default". Since the default
  pool is already btrfs, x-incus-storage: default on each service is sufficient
  — no changes needed to the volume declarations.

  But if the user wants to be explicit with btrfs snapshot scheduling on the
  volumes, that's the x-incus-snapshot extension. Let me update the compose file
  to be explicit about the btrfs pool and add snapshots:

  Read 1 file (ctrl+o to expand)
