  In the meantime — the correct approach from the schema: the UnixSocketPlugin
  reads /dev/shm/live-schema.json and reconciles sockets, while
  IncusPlugin.apply_state calls sync_devices to install the proxy devices. Both
  are driven by the schema example we already wrote. The manual incus config 
  device add I did earlier was the right call but was bypassing that system —
  the proper way is for op-dbus-mirror to apply the schema and let IncusPlugin
  install the devices automatically. The netmaker NIC issue is separate —
  netmaker needs at least one routable interface to start, which means the
  schema for the netmaker container should include a NIC device on the internal
  netmaker bridge, not zero NICs.

