❯ will it still have grpc payload?                                              

● Yes — XHTTP stream-up is just the transport layer (how bytes flow between xray
  nodes). The payload inside is whatever you want — gRPC, HTTP/1.1, MQTT, raw
  TCP. It's the same as how gRPC transport worked: a multiplexed H2 stream
  carrying arbitrary bytes.

  So:
  - netmaker REST API → still HTTP/1.1 payload, carried over H2 stream with path
  /api
  - MQTT → still MQTT protocol bytes, carried over H2 stream with path /mqtt
  - Actual gRPC services (op-grpc-bridge, qdrant) → gRPC payload, carried over
  H2 stream with path /grpc

  The transport switching from grpc → xhttp doesn't touch the payload at all.
  Want me to migrate the config?

