  which expects a VLESS+Reality client. Plain browsers get rejected. The browser
  needs to go through the mcp-socks SOCKS proxy (10.200.0.1:1081) which routes
  through mcp-reality outbound — that's the intended path for WG-connected
  browsers.

  The browser on the WG mesh needs to be configured to use the SOCKS proxy at
  10.200.0.1:1081. Is that proxy accessible from the WG client's perspective, or
  does the browser need a different entry point?

