● TCP connects but TLS handshake stalls — xray Reality is accepting the TCP
  connection then waiting for the Reality handshake, which a plain TLS client
  never sends. The connection just hangs instead of falling back.

  The VLESS+gRPC+Reality transport doesn't support TLS fallbacks the same way
  VLESS+TCP+TLS does. With network: grpc, there's no fallbacks mechanism — that
  only works with network: tcp. The actual inbound uses gRPC transport, which is
  why the fallbacks we added don't fire.

  To serve the dashboard to plain browsers, add a separate plain TLS inbound on
  a different port (e.g., 8080) with SNI routing, alongside the Reality inbound:

